<article class="entry entry-current">
  <h3 class="heading">Performance Analysis for HPC Systems Using Machine Learning</h3>
  <p class="time"><strong>Texas State University</strong> · Aug 2023 – Present</p>

  <p>
    Doctoral research building machine learning models that predict and explain performance on
    large-scale, DOE-class supercomputing systems — work carried out in direct collaboration with
    Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory.
  </p>

  <h4 class="subheading_h4">What the work involves</h4>
  <ul class="impact-list">
    <li>
      Led development of deep learning pipelines for HPC performance prediction, providing
      actionable insight for large-scale DOE-class computing systems.
    </li>
    <li>
      Collaborated with LLNL researchers to improve the efficiency and reliability of the Sierra
      HPC system through machine-learning-based optimization.
    </li>
    <li>
      Improved cross-platform prediction accuracy for new applications by 15% by developing more
      robust models — the kind of result that only comes from questioning the first model that
      works and testing whether it generalizes.
    </li>
    <li>
      Research outcomes published in top IEEE/ACM venues (COMPSAC, CCGRID, HPDC), recognized
      internationally, including an IEEE CCGRID Travel Grant.
    </li>
  </ul>
</article>
